  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1687 K, melting point of Si; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 12.082$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 14.272 + 0.388 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.781 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=14.272\\times10^{-3}T+0.194\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+1.781\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-4.870$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1687 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -29.100 + 0.250 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.477 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 11.300 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -29.100 - 0.250 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.477 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 5.650 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 0.259 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n1687-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -41.529 - 0.171 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.126 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 109.800 T^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -41.529 + 0.171 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.126 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 54.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 4.555 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Gurvich (49). ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase change: 1687 K, melting point of Si; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 12.082$ kcal/mol.",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 14.272 + 0.388 \\times 10^{-3} T - 1.781 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$",
      "$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=14.272\\times10^{-3}T+0.194\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+1.781\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-4.870$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "298.15-1687 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -29.100 + 0.250 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.477 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 11.300 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -29.100 - 0.250 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.477 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 5.650 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 0.259 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "1687-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -41.529 - 0.171 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.126 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 109.800 T^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -41.529 + 0.171 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.126 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 54.900 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 4.555 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "Source: Data from Gurvich (49)."
